# ── Firebase Secrets (NEVER commit these) ──────────────────────
# These files contain API keys and credentials.
# Copy the corresponding .example file, rename it (remove .example),
# and fill in your real values from the Firebase Console.
# See admin_dashboard/SETUP_GUIDE.md for step-by-step instructions.

# Flutter app credentials
lib/firebase_options.dart
android/app/google-services.json

# Admin dashboard credentials
admin_dashboard/firebase-config.js

# ── Firebase CLI artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────
# .firebaserc ties this repo to a specific Firebase project.
# It is safe to commit (contains no secrets — just the project ID).
# skills-lock.json and other tool-generated files should be ignored.
skills-lock.json

# ── IDE / AI tool config (not part of the project) ─────────────
.agents/
.claude/

# ── Large binary assets (videos & thumbnails) ──────────────────
# Videos are bundled into the APK at build time from local files.
# They should NOT be stored in git (too large; use LFS or just keep locally).
assets/videos/*.mp4
assets/videos/*.mov
assets/videos/*.avi

# Thumbnails CAN be committed (small images) — intentionally NOT ignored.
# If you prefer to keep them out of git too, uncomment:
# assets/thumbnails/*.jpg
# assets/thumbnails/*.png

